_url":"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/29891#issuecomment-1353265167","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/29891","id":1353265167,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCFbutM5QqTAP","user":{"login":"oaklandcorp-jkaiser","id":69987919,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5OTg3OTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69987919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser","html_url":"https://github.com/oaklandcorp-jkaiser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-12-15T15:26:40Z","updated_at":"2022-12-15T15:26:40Z","body":"> This is specific to using the Reactive stack. We don't promote the MariaDB dev service for reactive as we don't have an actual MariaDB reactive driver.\r\n> \r\n> My understanding is that the Reactive MySQL Client supports both MySQL and MariaDB so we should make it work.\r\n> \r\n> https://vertx.io/docs/vertx-mysql-client/java/#_mysql_and_mariadb_version_support_matrix\r\n> \r\n> I'll go do that.\r\n\r\nThat all makes sense. Thanks for the quick response and proposed fix!\r\n\r\nAfter recently discovering the power of dev services I've been trying to use them more in my development process. In other projects I've used `org.testcontainers.mariadb` directly in a `QuarkusTestResourceLifecycleManager` to include MariaDB containers in testing. That approach works fairly well for automated testing and doesn't require a ton of boilerplate but since dev services seems to be doing something similar under the seams it would be nicer if it could handle it. Plus then the application has the added bonus of using that container for dev mode testing and automated testing.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/1353265167/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"oaklandcorp-jkaiser","id":69987919,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5OTg3OTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69987919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser","html_url":"https://github.com/oaklandcorp-jkaiser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oaklandcorp-jkaiser/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":8056299271,"node_id":"CE_lADOCFbutM5ZUYVgzwAAAAHgMV8H","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/events/8056299271","actor":{"login":"geoand","id":4374975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNzQ5NzU